# Verible lint configuration. One reviewable place for every suppression, the
# same rule this repo applies to Verilator waivers, and every entry says why.
#
# Verible's default set encodes a SystemVerilog style guide. The RTL here is
# Verilog-2005 by design decision, so the rules that mandate SystemVerilog
# constructs cannot be satisfied and are not defects.

# Would require `always_comb`, which is SystemVerilog. Latch inference is
# instead prevented structurally by default-assigning every output at the top
# of each combinational block, and caught by `yosys check -assert`.
-always-comb

# Would require a storage type on a sized localparam, for which Verilog-2005
# offers no keyword: `logic` and `bit` are SystemVerilog. Unsized constants do
# carry `integer`, which the language does have.
-explicit-parameter-storage-type

# Expects CamelCase localparams, from the same SystemVerilog guide. This repo
# names constants in upper snake case throughout.
-parameter-name-style
